cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you cite this protocol or the accompanying code, please use the metadata below."
title: "When the power gate cannot fail: collapsed decision spaces defeat margin-and-power null reporting in LLM agents"
# This abstract must match the Abstract section of manuscript/main.md verbatim.
# analysis/scripts/check_claim_boundary.py compares them on every run, so editing
# one without the other fails repro.sh.
abstract: >-
  A common way to report a null in language-model evaluation pairs a materiality margin declared
  in advance with a power gate: the estimate must fall below the margin, and the design must have
  had the power to detect a shift of that size. We show that both guards can stop working at once,
  and in the same direction, when the categorical decision space partially collapses. In a
  completed measurement of an agent-internal channel over 4,800 draws, two of the five available
  zones are never produced at all. The power calculation takes the empirical read-out distribution
  as its base and builds its alternative by moving mass into the smallest cell, so a cell of
  probability exactly zero leaves the gate reporting 0.921 even at a hundredth of the declared
  margin of 0.10. The null floor of the distance statistic meanwhile stands at 0.027813, against
  an observed 0.038065. The channel is separately established as causal, separable and ablatable.
  This protocol estimates the same quantity in a second model family, to find out whether the
  failure mode belongs to the model or to the apparatus.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Miura"
    given-names: "Mikoto"
    alias: "mikotomiura"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-4196-0508"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
